{"title":"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The digits of a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are four consecutive integers in decreasing order when read from left to right. What is the sum of the possible remainders when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/78916550838bd31d66e4cdefbc366edb11fd00bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A brute-force solution to this question is fairly quick, but we'll try something slightly more clever:  our numbers have the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc7f8878efbeae0b35151755df4e13534407dfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\underline{(n+3)}}\\,{\\underline{(n+2)}}\\,{\\underline{( n+1)}}\\,{\\underline {(n)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"203\" height=\"21\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/7/1b789c5e99a61e65ce656a95d4abe26ca65cf791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 1000(n + 3) + 100(n + 2) + 10(n + 1) + n = 3210 + 1111n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"477\" height=\"18\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b8b5dcd9825c513d1437994e6930bea7ebdeea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in \\lbrace0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6\\rbrace$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/a/95a9e7b3c9d9dd1d21aca197af8264c89f53eaba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot 37 = 111$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/8/7782d881fa1654df5864754948126027d2fd3aef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 \\cdot 37 = 1110$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"109\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0bc210bb26756c96f08ba19e804565bd41bc64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90 \\cdot 37 = 3330$\" width=\"109\" height=\"12\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc2b71cebb6b8bfcc4b61bc58b95298d3bf2c79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$87 \\cdot 37 = 3219$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" />. So the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Remainder\" title=\"Remainder\">remainders</a> are all congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/d/a4d2871f3fffd9e218b9b2ea9a22d0c57973be51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 9 \\pmod{37}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" />. However, these numbers are negative for our choices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, so in fact the remainders must equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/6/2a62c50d87b35a62bccd21571026d772dd7ce5c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Adding these numbers up, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/557edb5db2f6402bfa463e386a523dcae0a5b1c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6) + 7\\cdot28 = \\boxed{217}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"337\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/6/ce6e98b5bc74e0816d00bc421ad6f6c2264cdc09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3210, 4321, 5432, \\cdots, 9876$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"207\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31be55cc25646bf2c630c8a0113532a122bb4e49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3210$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> gives a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/78916550838bd31d66e4cdefbc366edb11fd00bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />. To calculate the remainders of the other integers, notice that each number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/6/ac677f19229e898a89fb2dc6967d5232b8c62046.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1111$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> more than the previous number. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/6/ac677f19229e898a89fb2dc6967d5232b8c62046.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1111$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> gives a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/78916550838bd31d66e4cdefbc366edb11fd00bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />, the remainders of the other integers will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/cce449e0785c658fa4cf1776f19c8d6bde81bb38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29, 30, 31, \\cdots, 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/f/40ff2f1fc50c80bd4c287a19540494ea50440781.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28 + 29 + 30 + 31 + 32 + 33 + 34 = \\frac{28 + 34}{2} \\cdot 7 = \\boxed{217}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"434\" height=\"38\" />.\n~Viliciri\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I\" title=\"2004 AIME I\">2004 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2004\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202814\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.051 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 204/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1756/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 115/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4789/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.633      1 -total\n 58.05%    7.334      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.25%    4.958      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2681:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202814 and revision id 236086. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}